          {
            "commit": "e4ab8dc297b7cc216364fb6ef5792fbcbfe9143d",
            "subject": "LU-20439 lnet: consolidate existing peer in LNetAddPeer"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Jinshan Xiong",
          "email": "jinshanx@google.com",
          "date": "2026-06-17 05:15:53.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-07-10 17:35:00.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20409 lnet: Auto-bind NIs to local NUMA node by default",
        "message": "LU-20409 lnet: Auto-bind NIs to local NUMA node by default\n\nLNet now automatically binds each NI whose CPTs were not explicitly\nconfigured to the CPTs local to the NUMA node of its underlying\nhardware device. This prevents cross-NUMA performance degradation.\n\nEach LND records the CPT of its device in ni_dev_cpt during startup\n(e.g. derived from dev_to_node()), so the binding reuses that value\nrather than re-resolving the device: NIs are bound to every CPT\nsharing a NUMA node with ni_dev_cpt. LNDs without a backing device\nleave ni_dev_cpt as CFS_CPT_ANY and the NI is left on all CPTs.\n\nThe device's NUMA node is only known once the LND has opened the\ndevice during startup, but the LND also sizes its per-CPT scheduler\nthreads and memory pools against ni_cpts during that same startup,\nand ni_cpts must not be mutated once the NI is live on the receive\npath (lnet_nid2cpt() reads it locklessly). So each LND calls the new\nlnet_ni_set_default_cpts() helper itself, after it has determined\nni_dev_cpt and before it allocates those per-CPT resources. This\nkeeps the LND's footprint matched to the bound CPT set and finalizes\nni_cpts before the NI is published. The helper self-gates on NIs\nwith default CPTs, so lnet_startup_lndni() calls it only as a\nfallback for LNDs without a backing device (e.g. the loopback NI).\n\nNI allocation defers the net's CPT set for default NIs until the\nhelper runs. When the device's NUMA node already covers all CPTs the\nNI is left on the ni_cpts == NULL fast path. NIs with explicitly\nconfigured CPTs are unaffected.\n\nni_dev_cpt is now initialized to CFS_CPT_ANY in lnet_ni_alloc_common()\nso NIs whose LND never sets it are correctly treated as \"unknown\".\n\nRunning lnet_selftest without any configs on two 4-NUMA client nodes\nwith 200Gbps NIC over tcp.\nBefore this patch:\n[LNet Bandwidth of servers]\n[R] Avg: 12373.52 MiB/s Min: 12373.52 MiB/s Max: 12373.52 MiB/s\n[W] Avg: 12509.50 MiB/s Min: 12509.50 MiB/s Max: 12509.50 MiB/s\n\nAfter this patch:\n[LNet Bandwidth of servers]\n[R] Avg: 20374.35 MiB/s Min: 20374.35 MiB/s Max: 20374.35 MiB/s\n[W] Avg: 21736.28 MiB/s Min: 21736.28 MiB/s Max: 21736.28 MiB/s\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Jinshan Xiong <jinshanx@google.com>\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I6a7f58207003de59486aa01d1b90883ac8aeaa41\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66793\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
